{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"actinide-possible-scarab","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# 209 of 213 by-path test loaders are not cache-first, on keys shared by up to 9 files\n\n## Provenance\n\nMeasured by AST walk over `tests/` while auditing bug 2bc7 (which repaired three files sharing the\n`\"mutation\"` key). The audit's scope was that key; this is the surface it revealed.\n\n```\ntotal by-path loaders under tests/  : 213\nusing sys.modules.setdefault        :   0   (the original 9f0b/2bc7 defect is eradicated)\ncache-first (name AND __file__)     :   4\n```\n\nThe four are `test_differ.py`, `test_differ_conflict_resolution.py`,\n`test_differ_quarantine_suppression.py` (2bc7's three) and `test_reconcile_filter.py::_stub_modules`.\n2bc7 additionally fixed `test_differ_emits_probe.py` and `test_apply_list_of_mutations.py`.\n\n## The collision surface\n\n`sys.modules` keys registered by more than one test file:\n\n```\noutbound_differ   9 files        mutation    6 files\ninbound_differ    8 files        reconcile   4 files\ndiffer            5 files        applier     3 files\n```\n\n**None** of the loaders for `outbound_differ`, `inbound_differ`, `reconcile` or `applier` validates\n`__file__`. The original bug surfaced on `mutation` only because that is where a cross-file\n`isinstance` assertion happened to exist — the same latent coupling sits on keys with more registrants\nand no such assertion to expose it.\n\n## Why this is latent rather than broken\n\npytest executes module-by-module, so a file that overwrites a shared key is self-consistent while its\nown tests run: its module-scoped fixture was built when its registration was current. The failure needs\ntwo things to coincide — a cross-file identity comparison, and an execution order that puts the other\nregistrant first. 2bc7 was exactly that coincidence, and it presented as a macOS-only `isinstance`\nfailure on an object that WAS of the asserted class.\n\n## What 2bc7 deliberately did not attempt\n\nA shared helper, so the loader exists once. It is the right fix and it is not mechanical: the\nregistrants span `diffing/`, `mutate/`, `apply/`, `state/`, `fetch/`, `conflict/` and `orchestrate/`,\nand pytest puts only each test's OWN directory on `sys.path`, so a bare-name import does not resolve\nacross them. Two workable shapes, both with costs:\n\n* a module at the `tests/` root plus the `sys.path` plumbing `tests/_engine_path.py` already\n  establishes — works for every caller including module-level constants;\n* a conftest FIXTURE — inherited by subdirectories automatically, but cannot serve the call sites that\n  load at module scope, and several do.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] ONE cache-first by-path loader exists, reachable from every directory under `tests/` that needs\n      it, with the `sys.path` mechanism it depends on documented at its definition\n- [ ] every loader registering a key that MORE THAN ONE file registers is converted to it — the\n      `outbound_differ`, `inbound_differ`, `differ`, `mutation`, `reconcile` and `applier` keys at\n      minimum\n- [ ] a guard test fails when a new by-path loader registers a SHARED key without validating\n      `__file__`, so the count cannot regress silently (the audit above was a one-off scan; a scan\n      nobody re-runs is not a guard)\n- [ ] loaders that deliberately want an ISOLATED copy keep it, and say so — `test_mutation.py`\n      returns an unregistered private copy and `test_differ.py` registers\n      `mutation_for_diff_purity` under a distinct name; both are correct and must not be swept into\n      the shared helper\n- [ ] the full suite passes under a REVERSED collection order for the affected directories, not just\n      the default alphabetical one\n\n## Not urgent, and why\n\nNothing fails today. This is a latent-coupling cleanup whose value is that the next instance fails\nlocally and deterministically instead of as a platform-specific surprise in CI.","id":"e351-537e-a9ca-4669","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"209 of 213 by-path test loaders are not cache-first, on sys.modules keys shared by up to 9 files"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785866082318946001,"uuid":"ff756470-5c27-4a55-b0c9-139f3e584c12"}